  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining the Scene**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of Scene 1, focusing intently on the welcome sequence. I\'m taking the instructions and trying to envision the precise visual elements, like the minimal aesthetic, the animated envelope, and the glowing heart. I\'m focusing particularly on the user interaction with the \"Open Your Surprise\" button and what should happen on click.\n\n\n**Refining the Opening Scene**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the opening. I\'ve scrapped \"Read My Letter\" and am focused on a more concise opener: \"Someone has a special message for you...\" with a floating, animated envelope, and the glowing heart. The interaction is simplified to the button or envelope click to initiate the envelope animation, a smooth transition, and some light sound FX. I\'m imagining the effect now, focusing on the visual and UX flow. I need to make sure the clickable area is correct.\n\n\n**Celebrating Shared Moments**\n\nI am reflecting on the past year, filled with beautiful memories. I\'m filled with gratitude for the love and support. I feel blessed by our connection, and I hope we remain close through everything. I am hopeful for an even brighter future together and feel hopeful for more happy memories.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Visuals**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on Scene 3, analyzing the provided photographs and ensuring I use the correct assets. I\'m focusing on creating three Polaroid-style images with realistic shadows and a scrapbook-inspired composition. I\'m considering entrance animations, subtle parallax effects, and a responsive mobile layout. The critical aspect is to preserve the original images without any modification, and without creating any extra detail. I\'m focused on the user experience.\n\n\n**Crafting the Grand Finale**\n\nI\'m now deep in the final two scenes, Scene 4 and Scene 5. I\'m focusing on crafting a visually stunning anniversary reveal with animated hearts, confetti, and rose petals. I\'m aiming for an emotionally resonant, yet unobtrusive experience. The final scene needs a dreamy night-sky atmosphere, with animated hearts and a replay option. I\'ve noted the font requirements: Playfair Display for English headings, Hind Siliguri or Noto Serif Bengali for Bengali text, and Cormorant Garamond / Plus Jakarta Sans.\n\n\n**Implementing the Fonts**\n\nI\'ve just added the font imports for Playfair Display, Cormorant Garamond, Noto Serif Bengali, Hind Siliguri, and Plus Jakarta Sans to the `index.html` file. I\'ve also double-checked the `src/index.css` file to ensure the appropriate theme variables for fonts are correctly imported, so the design can be consistent.\n\n\n"
